---
source: crates/odx-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: cmd.render_long_help().to_string()
---
Bring an open migration up to date with what the addon got on the source series since: each new commit replayed with its author, bot commits left out, then odoo-lint's fixes for the target in a `[FW]` commit. On the migration branch checked out, or on someone else's migration pull request

Usage: odx migrate update [OPTIONS] [PR]

Arguments:
  [PR]
          A migration pull request to update instead of the branch checked out, for example `OCA/contract#1234`; its head becomes the local branch `<to>-mig-<addon>`

Options:
      --from <SERIES>
          The source series [default: the one recorded on the branch, else the series before the target]

      --remote <NAME>
          The remote the source series comes from [default: the one recorded on the branch, the one pointing at the pull request's repository, else `upstream` or `origin`]

      --since <COMMIT>
          The last commit of the source series the branch has, when odx cannot tell (a migration made in one commit)

      --no-squash
          Keep the administrative commits as they are

      --no-pre-commit
          Leave out the repository's pre-commit fixes

      --push
          Then push the branch where its pull request comes from

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -C, --project-dir <DIR>
          Run as if started in DIR

  -c, --config <FILE>
          The pyproject.toml to use (a repos.yaml for the commands that read one)

  -j, --jobs <N>
          Override the number of parallel jobs

      --offline
          Serve git repositories and forge and index data from the cache only; what is not cached fails. Local work (git, pre-commit, odoo-lint) takes as long as before

      --fresh
          Ignore cached data; refresh everything before answering

      --no-refresh
          Use cached data even when stale. Like --offline, this saves network time only

      --refresh-index
          Rebuild the addon index for the series involved

      --json
          Machine-readable output on stdout

  -v, --verbose...
          Say when each repository's fetch and build starts, and what each fetched and merged

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on standard error: no progress lines, no warnings
